{
 "case": "P02/E02 Anthropic × Messages failure and truncation terminals",
 "source": "Synthetic offline fixture. Terminals follow pi-ai 0.87.1 (commit 898ab804050730e9dcefb4443875d5a932aa6a32) packages/ai/src/api/anthropic-messages.ts: an HTTP error is the Anthropic TypeScript SDK's APIError message ('<status> <body message, else the body as JSON, else its text>', @anthropic-ai/sdk core/error.js makeMessage); an SSE error event throws its data; message_start without message_stop, a missing stop reason, an unhandled stop reason and a mid-output fallback throw pi's own texts; refusal and sensitive map to error with pi's messages (pi tests: preserves refusal stop details, preserves sensitive stop reasons); max_tokens is the length terminal. Texts pi takes from Node.js (JSON.parse, undici's 'terminated') are barness's fixed texts, recorded in the pi ledger.",
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "id": "http-401",
